1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,914
A neighbor in the dormitory, a careful woman who had never once complained, asked to speak to the group.

2
00:00:06,914 --> 00:00:20,652
She was a delegate from the night shift, and her story had no art in it: an alcoholic father, a mother who worked six days a week, and a brother who had left school at fifteen.

3
00:00:20,652 --> 00:00:24,246
“I do not hate them,” she said.

4
00:00:24,246 --> 00:00:36,020
“I just remember everything.” Six months ago the project had one voice; see how a single person can change the parent document.

5
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:42,614
Her expression did not change when she described the accident, but her hands did.

6
00:00:42,614 --> 00:00:58,232
“There was no violence in our house,” she said, “only a fright every evening.” The group had expected a story about money; what emerged was a story about a clock, a lap, and a chair by the window.

7
00:00:58,232 --> 00:01:02,796
“So the survey missed the substance,” Maya said.

8
00:01:02,796 --> 00:01:10,535
However, the information was still thin, and not one word of it had been checked.

9
00:01:10,535 --> 00:01:16,449
The dominant voice in the room had always belonged to people with qualifications.

10
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:22,529
“A qualification is a permission, not a person,” the woman said.

11
00:01:22,529 --> 00:01:37,926
“Do not be a coward about the scope.” A thoughtful word, a homely detail, a neat list of small comforts: the group wrote them down with the devotion of students who had learned to listen.

12
00:01:37,926 --> 00:01:43,486
The palace of theory was immune to such evidence, and that was the sting.

13
00:01:43,486 --> 00:01:50,550
“An intellectual project that cannot communicate grief is a bore,” Professor Zhao said.

14
00:01:50,550 --> 00:02:02,958
“Not a failure — a bore.” The sting of the word angered Maya, and she was careless about her own tone in reply; the black coat made her look older than she was.

15
00:02:02,958 --> 00:02:09,937
“Any of you would have done the same,” she said, and regretted it at once.

16
00:02:09,937 --> 00:02:15,252
They invited the woman to sit on the panel and allowed her to set the agenda.

17
00:02:15,252 --> 00:02:25,060
She stimulated one change immediately: the survey would ask what people tend in their own homes, not what they wear to the interview.

18
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:30,360
“There is a probable reason nobody asked before,” Lin wrote.

19
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:46,583
“The people who write surveys are the people who answer them.” His mother telephoned that evening, and he told her about the woman; she said only, “Good,” which was, from her, a long speech.

20
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:54,027
A conscientious student would have apologized at once; the shame of the moment was that she had not.

21
00:02:54,027 --> 00:03:07,604
A charitable reading was possible, but it did not make the room any warmer, and the dominance of the loudest voice in it was itself a kind of violence that no contemporary account would ever record.

22
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:12,919
She had seen enough suffering to know the difference.
